  "termsS1Title": "What TeleMonitor is",
  "termsS1P1": "TeleMonitor helps you follow your blood pressure and blood sugar at home with your clinician. You enter your readings; the app compares them with your home targets and your clinician reviews the alerts.",
  "termsS1P2": "TeleMonitor does not replace a consultation and is not an emergency service. It never changes your treatment: only your clinician can. If you feel very unwell, go to the nearest health centre or hospital without waiting for an answer in the app.",
  "termsS2Title": "The information the app keeps",
  "termsS2B1": "• Your account: name and email address.",
  "termsS2B2": "• Your profile, if you fill it in: age, sex, height, weight, conditions, medications, phone, emergency contact and an optional photo.",
  "termsS2B3": "• Your readings (blood pressure, heart rate, blood sugar, when you measured and your notes), the alerts they raise and your clinician's review of them.",
  "termsS2B4": "• If you measure your pulse with the phone camera, the pulse found: the images of the camera are read on the phone and dropped at once, never kept or sent.",
  "termsS2B5": "• The messages you exchange with your clinician.",
  "termsS2B6": "• What the service needs to work: when you last used the app, and the address used to send notifications to your phone.",
  "termsS3Title": "Who can see it",
  "termsS3B1": "• You.",
  "termsS3B2": "• The clinician you connect to, and the colleague they name to replace them when an alert waits too long.",
  "termsS3B3": "• The administrator of the system, only to keep it working.",
  "termsS3P1": "Your information is stored on Google Firebase servers and travels encrypted. Access rules let each person see only what they are allowed to see.",
  "termsS3P2": "When you use the health assistant, your question, age, sex, conditions, medications and recent readings are sent to Google's Gemini service to prepare the answer, never your name or contact details. Do not type your name or other personal details in the assistant.",
  "termsS4Title": "Research, only if you agree",
  "termsS4P1": "If you tick the research box, your information may also be used for medical research on the home follow-up of hypertension and diabetes, by the TeleMonitor project of the GISDIA laboratory, National Higher Polytechnic School of Douala (ENSPD), University of Douala.",
  "termsS4P2": "Before any use, your name, email, phone numbers, emergency contact, photo, messages and notes are removed, and your account is replaced by a code. Results are published only as figures about groups of patients, in which no one can be recognised.",
  "termsS4P3": "Saying no changes nothing in your care. You can change your choice at any time in your profile; from then on, your information is left out of new research extracts.",
  "termsS5Title": "Your rights",
  "termsS5P1": "Under Law No. 2024/017 of 23 December 2024 on the protection of personal data in Cameroon, you can see your information (the app shows it to you), have it corrected, withdraw your research consent, and ask for your account and your information to be deleted. For a deletion or any question, ask your clinician or the administrator.",
  "termsS6Title": "Keeping your account safe",
  "termsS6P1": "Keep your password to yourself. Confirm your email address: it is the only way to set a new password if you forget yours. On a shared phone, sign out when you finish.",
  "termsS7Title": "Changes to these terms",
  "termsS7P1": "If these terms change, the app shows you the new version and asks you to accept it before you continue.",
